{"id":"u-7a111f3c-b917-45a4-adeb-a53ad6f9a759","src":"community","title":"Juggernaut Method – Powerbuilding 4 Days","author":"Manuel B.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/8Zpifq-juggernaut-method","desc":"A 16-week powerbuilding program built around the 10s, 8s, 5s and 3s wave progression of the Juggernaut Method.\n\nThe program combines structured strength progression on the four main lifts — Bench Press, Squat, Overhead Press and Deadlift — with hypertrophy-focused accessory work using a simple total-rep progression system.\n\nEach 4-week wave consists of Accumulation, Intensification, Realization and Deload.\n\nThe final “+ set” is autoregulated throughout each wave:\n\nAccumulation: stop with 2–3 reps in reserve\nIntensification: stop with 1–2 reps in reserve\nRealization: 0 RIR / maximum quality reps\nDeload: no + sets\n\nPerformance during the Realization week is used to adjust the Training Max for the following wave, allowing progression to reflect actual performance rather than relying solely on predetermined load increases.\n\nAccessory Progression\n\nEach workout contains one main lift and three accessory movements.\n\nAccessories use total rep goals based on exercise type and fatigue:\n\n30 reps — heavier compound movements\n40 reps — moderate-load compounds and machine movements\n50 reps — isolation and low-fatigue movements\n\nChoose a load that initially requires approximately 4 sets to complete the prescribed total reps.\n\nOnce the full rep goal can be completed in 3 clean sets at the prescribed effort, increase the load and build back up again.\n\nRest Periods\n\nMain Lifts: 4 minutes\n30 Rep Goal: 2:30\n40 Rep Goal: 2:00\n50 Rep Goal: 1:30\n\nRamp-up sets begin with approximately 1:30 rest, adding around 30 seconds as intensity increases.\n\nWho is it for?\n\nDesigned for intermediate lifters who want to build muscle without putting strength development on the back burner.\n\nThe program provides substantial work on the competition-style lifts while using bodybuilding-oriented accessories to develop a balanced physique, with additional emphasis on chest development.","level":["Intermediate","Novice"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":20,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-11-02T00:14:04.347Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Bench","Squat","Military Press","Deadlift"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":60,"x":5}],"note":"LAST SET:\nAMRAP RIR 2-3"},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":30,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"2'30\""},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":30,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"2'30\""},{"n":"Bicep Curl (EZ Bar)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":60,"x":5}],"note":"LAST SET:\nAMRAP RIR 2-3"},{"n":"Single Leg Extension","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""},{"n":"Single-Leg Leg Curl","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""},{"n":"Cable Crunch","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Military Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":60,"x":5}],"note":"LAST SET:\nAMRAP RIR 2-3"},{"n":"Inclined DB Press","sets":[{"max":1,"r":40,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"2'"},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Cable)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""},{"n":"Tricep Pushdown (Cable)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"pct":60,"x":5}],"note":"LAST SET:\nAMRAP RIR 2-3"},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":30,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"2'30\""},{"n":"Pendlay Row","sets":[{"max":1,"r":40,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9}],"note":"2'"},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"max":1,"r":50,"rpe":9}],"note":"1'30\""}]}],[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"pct":55},{"r":5,"pct":62.5},{"r":10,"pct":67.5,"x":3}],"note":"LAST SET: AMRAP RIR 1-2\nRAMP: 1'30\" +@30\"\nWORK: 4'"},{"n":"Incline Bench Pre